<title>CHILE: RESEARCH ALERT-Banco Santiago upgraded.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Banco Santiago upgraded.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>ING Barings upgraded Banco Santiago to hold from sell.</p>
<p>Analysts Nuno Fernandes and Petru Vaduva cited Santiago's strong price decline since March, saying it underperformed the Chilean market by 11 percent in the past month.</p>
<p>They also cited weaker bottom-line first quarter earnings due to higher-than-expected expenses related to the merger with Banco O'Higgins last year.</p>
<p>They lowered their estimate of earnings per American Depositary Receipt to $1.87 and $2.33 in 1997 and 1998, from $2.18 and $2.41, respectively.</p>
<p>((--Roger Atwood, Santiago newsroom +56-2-699-5595 x211))</p>
